%description:

Tcp.tlpEnabled:on-loss-response -- when the probe repaired a lost tail, the window drops to the threshold.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Tail Loss Probe (RFC 8985 section 7)"; RFC 8985 section 7.4.2:
when an ACK covers data after the probe and no D-SACK shows that both copies arrived, the probe
repaired a loss, and the sender invokes the congestion response.

The class on-loss-response: TcpAlgorithmBase::processTlpAck() calls tlpLossResponse(), which
sets the threshold for a fast recovery and the window to it. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "on" from
"off", where no probe goes.

Host under test: host1, with a link delay of 10 ms; host1 sends 4344 bytes (3 segments) at
0.2 s and 1448 bytes at 1.5 s, and the tap drops the third segment the first time.
Observation: level 1 and 2, the probe sends the third segment again, and at the ACK of the
data of 1.5 s a threshold comes.

%# parameter: Tcp.tlpEnabled
%# class: on-loss-response
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpTlpEnabledOnLossResponse")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the third data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the third data segment of host1")
             .within(2.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the probe: the third segment again")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 5792")
             .describe("the ACK of the data of 1.5 s")
             .within(1.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .describe("the threshold of the loss response")
                  .within(0.01));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpTlpEnabledOnLossResponse compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendScript = "0.2 4344; 1.5 1448"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 0B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpTlpEnabledOnLossResponse: PASS
